#. module: treasury_forecast_project
#: model:ir.model.fields,help:treasury_forecast_project.field_project_project__treasury_margin_calculation
msgid ""
"Choose how the sale price is calculated for this project.\n"
"\n"
"Margin on Cost Price:\n"
"Sale Price = Cost Price * (1 + Margin / 100)\n"
"Example: Cost 100, Margin 20% -> Sale Price 120.\n"
"\n"
"Margin on Sale Price:\n"
"Sale Price = Cost Price / (1 - Margin / 100)\n"
"Example: Cost 100, Margin 20% -> Sale Price 125.\n"
"\n"
"The default method is taken from the company settings, but it can be changed for each project."
msgstr ""

#. module: treasury_forecast_project
#: model:ir.model.fields,help:treasury_forecast_project.field_res_company__treasury_margin_calculation
msgid ""
"Choose how the sale price is calculated from the cost price and the margin.\n"
"\n"
"Margin on Cost Price:\n"
"Sale Price = Cost Price * (1 + Margin / 100)\n"
"Example: Cost 100, Margin 20% -> Sale Price 120.\n"
"\n"
"Margin on Sale Price:\n"
"Sale Price = Cost Price / (1 - Margin / 100)\n"
"Example: Cost 100, Margin 20% -> Sale Price 125.\n"
"\n"
"This calculation applies to treasury forecasts linked to a project when the category type is 'Both'."
msgstr ""

